p_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":0.004213925645872716,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":21.2,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.09781183646352026,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":86.3,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.04293760882697556,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":46.3,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.02222499054747118,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":31.1,"_gate_rev_durability":0.03932918710699518,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":44.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.007562032078013022,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":19.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.040815127470477,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.025144054478784705,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":58.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.011360001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.429,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":42.9,"pf":[],"description_full":"Aon plc operates as a professional services company in the United States, rest of the Americas, the United Kingdom, Ireland, rest of Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. It operates through two segments, Risk Capital and Human Capital. The company offers commercial risk solutions comprising retail and insurance brokerage, specialty solutions, global risk consulting, captives management, and affinity programs; health solutions, such as consulting and brokerage, consumer benefits, and talent advisory services; and wealth solutions, including retirement consulting and investments. It also provides treaty and facultative reinsurance; strategy and technology group solutions; insurance-linked securities, capital raising, strategic advice, restructuring, and merger and acquisition services; and risk management products and solutions, capital market solutions, and corporate finance advisory services. In addition, the company offers strategic design advice and actuarial services; pension risk transfer and integrated pension administration; and investment advisory services on developing and maintaining investment programs across various plan types, including defined benefit plans, defined contribution plans, master trusts, and pooled employer plans for corporations, public pensions, endowments, and foundations. Aon plc was incorporated in 1979 and is headquartered in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Andrew  Marcell | Deputy CEO and Senior EVP of Risk Capital & Human Capital | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 60K people. Revenue per employee of $286K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $54K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Aon plc is a large-cap financial services business with a $73.9B market cap on $17.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $3.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.94\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.8%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Carries a 40% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.40295660467334304},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Large open-market insider purchases (net $3.5M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Here's Why Investors Should Stay Neutral on AON Stock for Now","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036819/here-s-why-investors-should-stay-neutral-on-aon-stock-for-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Crank_focused-3036819","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795796100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Why Is Aon (AON) Up 8% Since Last Earnings Report?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036747/why-is-aon-aon-up-8-since-last-earnings-report?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3036747","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795793412.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Aon President Michael Sicard Reports 148,348 Restricted Shares Following USI Merger Closure","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/aon-president-michael-sicard-reports-148348-restricted-shares-following-usi-merger-closure","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795786268.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"ETFs Are Net Sellers of Aon (AON) on Nov. 25","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/etfs-net-sellers-aon-aon-110215985.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795777335.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Aon (AON) Undervalued On Stronger Risk Advisory Demand And Digital Claims Progress?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-aon/aon/news/is-aon-aon-undervalued-on-stronger-risk-advisory-demand-and","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795673619.992,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MS Global Franchise Portfolio's Top Q3 2026 Move: A